  "result": "`click.KeyValue` now exists and works as `@click.option('--set', type=click.KeyValue())`. The full test suite passes.\n\n- **Parsing:** it splits on the first `=`, so `a=b=c` gives `('a', 'b=c')` and `a=` gives `('a', '')`.\n- **Errors:** input with no `=`, an empty key (`=value`), or an empty string fails with `'...' is not a valid key=value pair.`\n- **Code:** the class is in `src/click/types.py` and exported from `src/click/__init__.py`.\n- **Tests:** I added tests next to the related ones in `tests/test_types.py`.\n- **Docs and changelog:** I added entries to `docs/api.md` and `docs/parameter-types.md`. `CHANGES.md` had no unreleased section, so I created \"Version 8.6.0 / Unreleased\" for the new entry. Rename that heading if you want a different version number.\n\nI didn't commit anything.",
